  "method": {
    "command": "build/windows/bench/ninfer_peer_transfer_pipeline_bench.exe 32 31",
    "samples": "31 rotated paired batches per route, 32 consecutive collectives per batch, eight warmups, normal and reversed device order",
    "metrics": "Host enqueue, complete wall, and origin-GPU event interval joined after both complete sums, reported separately. All timing inputs are initialized to zero outside the interval; separate changing nonzero qualification is mandatory.",
    "ownership": "Private owner supplies one nonblocking D2H stream per rank, producer/tile-ready/pull-done events, and portable pinned buffers with guards; no hot-path allocations.",
    "ordering": "Publish both ranks current producer and tile-ready records; main streams pull peer tiles; both pull-done records precede main joins of own final D2H and peer H2D. Then launch unchanged full-buffer residual_add once per rank. All auxiliary uses retire into main-stream order.",
    "oracle": "Full-coordinate/rank/call/epoch-decorrelated represented BF16 operands. Independent FP64 sum for every output; bounded dyadic sums are exactly FP32-representable before final BF16 RNE. All routes pass the same exact oracle.",
    "checks": "Every changing output and pinned publication, final incoming scratch, device/host guards, four calls without host synchronization per epoch, alternating producer skew, mixed public/private calls, both GPU orders, owner destroyed with pending work, resident outputs checked after every timing batch."
  },
